# Architecture Patterns
- Use functional components with hooks
- Follow feature-based folder structure
- Implement error boundaries for async operations
- Use custom hooks for shared logic

# Code Style Conventions
- Use named exports over default exports
- Prefer const over let, avoid var
- Use async/await over promises chains
- Keep functions under 50 lines when possible
- Use descriptive variable names (no single letters except iterators)

# File Naming
- Components: PascalCase (UserProfile.tsx)
- Utilities: camelCase (formatDate.ts)
- Constants: UPPER_SNAKE_CASE (API_ENDPOINTS.ts)
- Hooks: camelCase with 'use' prefix (useAuth.ts)

# Import Order
1. React/Framework imports
2. Third-party libraries
3. Internal components
4. Utilities/Helpers
5. Types/Interfaces
6. Styles

# Testing Requirements
- Unit tests for utilities and hooks
- Component tests for UI components
- Integration tests for critical flows
- E2E tests for main user journeys

# Don't Do This
- Don't use 'any' type in JavaScript
- Don't directly mutate state
- Don't ignore JavaScript errors
- Don't skip error handling
- Don't commit console.logs
- Don't create god components (>300 lines)

# Always Do This
- Add JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Handle loading and error states
- Implement proper JavaScript types
- Write tests alongside features
- Follow accessibility guidelines (a11y)
- Use semantic HTML

